meta {
  name: Get Nearest Place By Coordinate
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/trip/coordinate/nearest/:coordinate
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  coordinate: -6.177464532426197,106.7912179194768
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Get Nearest Place By Coordinate

  This request is used to get nearest place (trip destination or trip origin name). This request interacts with the MySQL database, has protected routes, and a pagination.

  ## Path Parameters

  | Name       | Type   | Required | Description         | Example                              |
  |------------|--------|----------|-----------------------|----------------------------------------|
  | coordinate | string | yes      | Latitude,longitude   | -6.177464532426197,106.7912179194768 |

  ## Responses

  **200 — Trip fetched successfully.** Ordered in descending order by `distance`
```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "trip fetched",
    "data": {
      "current_page": 1,
      "data": [
        {
          "id": "28668090-5653-dff5-2d8f-af603fc36b45",
          "place_name": "Location A",
          "place_coordinate": "-6.177464532426197, 106.7912179194768",
          "place_distance": 20,
          "last_visit": "2025-06-19 07:54:42"
        }
      ],
      "last_page": 1,
      "per_page": 14,
      "total": 1
    }
  }
```

  **401 — protected route need to include sign in token as authorization bearer**
```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "you need to include the authorization token from login"
  }
```

  **404 — trip failed to fetched**
```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "trip not found"
  }
```

  **500 — Internal Server Error**
```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "something wrong. please contact admin"
  }
```
}